52 series, 104 units"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPM-011"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.867, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-044 (0.74); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-044", "FAM:SF-APPA-050 auto_related_family (record_link_extends) FAM:SF-APPA-058"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "score": 0.828, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-083 (0.72); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-083", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.75); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.", "observed_result": "Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n>=30 for lineup cells cited", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-054", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-054: PUTBACK suppression mechanism: fatigue vs value", "score": 0.774, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-050 auto_related_family (record_link_extends) FAM:SF-APPA-054", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.75); FAM:SF-APPA-054 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "PUTBACK suppression mechanism: fatigue vs value", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "PUTBACK suppresses the next star possession via fatigue (stronger in H2 and Q4), while PUTBACK itself remains high-value.", "observed_result": "H1 delta -0.038 vs H2 -0.130 (22 stars, 3.4x). Q1 -0.009 vs Q4 -0.289 (11 stars; Q4 pooled n=34). PUTBACK H2 1.528 vs 1.217 (+0.311) n=8,614 vs 474,564. After opp PUTBACK offense 1.097 vs 1.210 (d=-0.113) n=15,898.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Q4 PUTBACK is sparse (34 pooled poss at n>=30; Mitchell n=34 drives the Q4 cell) even though the H2 vs H1 and aftershock tests are larger.", "observed_verdict": "supported"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:insufficient_exposure"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-050"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-055", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-055: All play types x Q1-Q4 gradient on 30 stars", "score": 0.774, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-050 auto_related_family (record_link_extends) FAM:SF-APPA-055", "request matches DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups (0.75); FAM:SF-APPA-055 auto_uses_dataset DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "All play types x Q1-Q4 gradient on 30 stars", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Only PUTBACK shows a fatigue signature (near-zero Q1 suppression compounding to Q4) across the full 30-star panel.", "observed_result": "PUTBACK Q1 d=-0.001 to Q4 d=-0.233, Q1->Q4 -0.232 (Q1 poss 722 / Q4 531). Other PTs suppress in Q1 already; largest other gradient DRIVE -0.060. CUT reverses +0.020. TRANSITION -0.053.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "On the full 30-star weighted panel, only PUTBACK is near-zero in Q1 and heavy in Q4.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars; PUTBACK Q4 n=531 poss", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "supported"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-050"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-054"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-056"}]}], "n_results": 10}

